      "id": 1,
      "text": "Limerick was named after County Limerick in Ireland, where many railroad workers who settled in the neighborhood came from.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.udstudio.org/stories/limerick-stroll",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1879 the neighborhood’s historic campus land was purchased and became Kentucky’s first post‑secondary school for African Americans, the Kentucky Normal and Theological Institute.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.udstudio.org/stories/limerick-stroll",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Simmons College of Kentucky, founded on that campus, today is a member of the Historically Black Colleges and Universities community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.udstudio.org/stories/limerick-stroll",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "A historic baseball alley in Limerick once ran along Kentucky Street, the site of Louisville’s early Major League team, the Eclipse, later the Colonels.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
